$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a stirred solution of 4-nitrobenzylaldehyde
(0.302 g, 2 mmol), aqueous trimethylamine (0.5 mL, 2.5 mmol) in methanol
(2 mL) was added acrylonitrile (0.40 mL, 6 mmol). The resulting clear
mixture was stirred at room temperature for 0.5h (monitored by TLC). Then
chloroform (20 mL) and water (5 mL) were added and the mixture was
stirred for another 2 min. The organic phase was separated and the water
phase was extracted with chloroform (2 x10 mL). The combined organic
phase was dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate. After removing of the
solvent and low bolting-point substance the crude product was purified by
column chromatography to afford the pure adduct. 1k, colorless liquid,
yield 88%, nD20 1.5354. 1H NMR(δ, CDCl3): 2.83(br., OH), 3.70(s, 3H),
5.54(s, 1H), 5.81(s, 1H), 6.32(s, 1H), 7.15~7.64(m, 5H). Anal. Calculated
for C11H12O3: C, 68.74; H, 6.29. Found: C, 68.45; H, 6.25.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Dramatic Rate Acceleration of the Baylis-Hillman Reaction in Homogeneous
Medium in the Presence of Water
