$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Baylis-Hillman
Reaction Leading to Adducts (4). Method 1. In a one-necked flask (25 mL)
the appropriate aldehyde (10.0 mmol), ethyl or methyl acrylate (10.0
mmol) and DABCO (0.11 g, 1.0 mmol) were added and the mixture was allowed
to react for 96 h at rt. The oil was then purified by silica gel
chromatography (cyclohexane:ethyl acetate 80:20) to give pure adducts 4.
Methyl 3-hydroxy-3-phenyl-2-methylenepropanoate (4a), (1.62 g, 86%) as a
colorless oil. EI MS: m/z (rel intens) 192 (100, M+), 175 (36), 160 (50),
159 (52), 132 (94), 105 (92). Anal. Calcd for C11H12O3 : C, 68.74; H,
6.29. Found: C, 68.69; H, 6.25.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction
