$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3.1. Synthesis of Methyl 3-Hydroxy-3-phenylacrylate (7) 5 A mixture of
methyl acrylate (15.0 g, 174 mmol), benzaldhyde (15.0g, 141 mmol) and
DABCO (15.9 g, 141 mmol) was stirred at room temperature for 3 days, and
then 150 mL of ether was added. The organic layer was separated and
washed with dilute HCl, aq NaHCO3 and water, and then dried over Na2SO4.
After removal of the volatile, the residue was purified by column
chromatography (silica gel, ethyl acetate/hexanes, 11/10) to afford 23.1
g (85% yields) of the target product as oil.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
