$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 3-hydroxy-2-methylene-3-phenylpropanoate (18f). Purification by
column chromatography (3:1 hexane/EtOAc) afforded a desired compound 18f
(149 mg, 77%) as a colorless liquid. Spectral data were identical to
those previously reported.1 TLC: R f 0.50 (3:1 hexane/EtOAc). 1H-NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.40-7.29 (m, 5H), 6.34 (s, 1H), 5.83 (s, 1H), 5.58 (d,
1H, J = 5.6 Hz), 3.73 (s, 3H), 2.98 (d, 1H, J = 5.6 Hz). 13C-NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ 166.9, 142.2, 141.5, 128.6, 128.0, 126.8, 126.2, 73.3,
52.1. LRMS (FAB) m/z (rel int): 175 ([M-OH]+, 77), 215 ([M+Na]+, 20).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction, 1-butyl-3-methyltriazolium hexafluorophosphate
as solvent gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 1,3-Dialkyl-1,2,3-triazolium Ionic Liquids and Their
Applications to the Baylis-Hillman Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Jeong, Yunkyung; Ryu, Jae-Sang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2010), 75(12), 4183-4191

