$DATUM 280-57-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the preparation of Baylis-Hillman adducts 1a, 1c-f.
A mixture of acrylate (or methyl vinylketone) (100 mmol), aldehyde (130
mmol) and DABCO (1,4-diazabicyclo[2.2.2]octane) (20 mmol) was stirred for
3-5 days and then diluted with EtOAc. The reaction was washed twice with
1M HCl, dried over MgSO4 and concentrated. The crude was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel using hexanes-ethyl acetate as
eluent. Methyl 3-hydroxy-3-phenyl-2-methylene-propanoate 1a: 75%
colorless oil. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.00 (bs, 1H, OH), 3.74 (s, 3H),
5.58 (s,. 1H), 5.84 (s, 1H), 6.35 (s, 1H), 7.27- 7.40 (m, 5H). 13C NMR
(125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 51.9, , 73.2, 126.0, 126.7, 127.8, 128.5, 141.5,
142.2, 166.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Magnesium Bromide Mediated Highly Diastereoselective Heterogeneous
Hydrogenation of Olefins
