$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the asymmetric addition
of n-BuLi to aldehyde. In a flame-dried round-bottom flask containing a
magnetic stirring bar, chiral amine 8 (0.33 g, 1.1 mmol) was dissolved in
dry pentane (10 mL) under an argon atmosphere. The solution was cooled to
-78 °C in a dry ice acetone cooling bath and n-BuLi (0.61 mL, 1.6 mmol)
was added dropwise. The reaction mixture was then kept at room
temperature for 20 minutes. The mixture was cooled to -116 °C in a liquid
nitrogen and ethanol cooling bath and equilibrated for 20 minutes before
a solution of benzaldehyde (0.022 mL, 0.22 mmol) in pentane was added
either dropwise via a syringe pump (3.0 mL pentane) or all at once (0.4
mL pentane). After 1 hour, the reaction was quenched with methanol (0.5
mL) and allowed to reach room temperature before it was separated between
saturated ammonium chloride aqueous solution and dichloromethane. The
combined organic layer was dried over sodium sulfate and solvent
evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude product was further purified
with column chromatography and gave colorless oil. The enantiomeric
excesses were analyzed by GC.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 74% ee, slow addn. of aldehyde, aldehyde addn. in one
portion gave lower ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Analysis of an Asymmetric Addition with a 2:1 Mixed Lithium
Amide/n-Butyllithium Aggregate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Liu, Jia; Li, Deyu; Sun, Chengzao; Williard, Paul G.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2008), 73(11), 4045-4052

