$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a suspension of NaH (233 mg, 5.82 mmol) in THF (10 mL) was added a
solution of 11 (840 mg, 5.83 mmol) in THF (8 mL + two 1 mL rinses) at 0°C
under argon. After 15 min, the mixture was cooled to -78°C and a solution
of n-BuLi (2.50 mL, 5.62 mmol, 2.25 M in hexanes) was added. After 1 h,
the reaction mixture was allowed to warm to -10 °C for 10 min and was
then cooled to -78°C. To this mixture was added a solution of 10 (605 mg,
2.56 mmol) in THF (8 mL + two 1 mL rinses). After 45 min, the reaction
was quenched with half saturated aqueous NH4Cl (100 mL) and diluted with
Et2O (50 mL). The two layers were separated and the organic layer was
washed with H2O (50 mL) and brine (50 mL). The organic layer was dried,
filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The products were purified by column
chromatography (35% Et2O in hexanes) to give 761 mg (78%) of a mixture of
diastereomers that were taken on without full characterization.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
