$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Allylic alcohol rac -8 Vinylmagnesium bromide (1.0 M in THF, 119 mL, 119
mmol) was added dropwise to a stirred solution of p-nitrobenzaldehyde
(15.1 g, 99.9 mmol) in anhydrous THF (350 mL). The solution was stirred
for 2 hours at -78 °C. Saturated aqueous ammonium chloride (300 mL) was
then slowly added to quench the solution and the mixture was extracted
with ethyl acetate (3 × 250 mL). The combined organic layers were washed
with water (200 mL) and brine (300 mL). The organic layers were then
dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered and the solvent was removed under
reduced pressure. The residue which resulted was purified by flash
chromatography (3:97→15:85 ethyl acetate/hexanes). rac -8 as a yellow
crystalline solid (13.2 g, 74%). m.p. 50-51 °C [lit.1 m.p. 48-49 °C]; 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.20 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H, p-nitrophenyl), 7.55 (d,
J = 8.3 Hz, 2H, p-nitrophenyl), 5.98 (ddd, J = 16.8, 10.2, 6.5 Hz, 1H,
CH=CH2), 5.43-5.25 (m, 3H, OCH and CH2), 2.13 (d, J = 3.56 Hz, 1H, OH);
13C {1H} NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 149.5, 147.3, 139.1, 126.9, 123.7, 116.8,
74.6; MS (APCI, +ve) m/z 181 (7%, MH+); 1H NMR data in accordance with
literature values.2
