$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(2-Methoxy-phenyl)-prop-2-en-1-ol (1a): To a solution of
2-methoxy-benzaldehyde (1.20 mL, 10.0 mmol) in ether (25 mL) was added a
solution of vinyl magnesiumchloride in THF (1.7 M, 7.6 mL, 13 mmol) at
0°C. The mixture was stirred for 30 min., diluted with ether and poured
onto aqueous NH4Cl solution. The organic layer was separated, and the
aqueous layer was extracted twice with MTBE. The combined organic
extracts were dried with MgSO4, filtered, and the solvent was evaporated
under reduced pressure. The residue was distilled (0.1 mbar, bp 95°C).
1-(2-Methoxy-phenyl)-prop-2-en-1-ol (1a), yield 1.50 g, 91%. 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 2.81 (s, 1 H), 3.87 (s, 3 H), 5.17 (d, J = 10.5 Hz, 1
H), 5.32 (d, J = 17.2 Hz, 1 H), 5.41 (dd, J = 6.2, 5.5 Hz, 1 H), 6.14
(ddd, J = 17.2, 10.5, 5.5 Hz, 1 H), 6.90 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1 H), 6.96 (dd,
J = 7.5, 7.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.27 (ddd, J = 7.7, 7.5, 1.7 Hz, 1 H), 7.31 (dd, J
= 7.5, 1.3 Hz, 1 H) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 55.3 (3), 71.6
(1), 110.7 (1), 114.5 (2), 120.9 (1), 127.4 (1), 128.7 (1), 130.7 (0),
139.4 (1), 158.2 (0) ppm. IR (film, KBr-plates): ν = 1491 (s), 1651 (s),
3419 (s) cm-1. MS (EI): m/z = 164 (78) [M+], 107 (100). C10H12O2 (164.2):
calcd. C 73.2, H 7.4; found: C 72.7, H 7.3.
