$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for the allylation of
aldehydes promoted by P4a: To a suspension of P4a (164 mg, 0.6 mmol) in
acetonitrile (1.5 mL) were added successively benzaldehyde (53 mg, 0.5
mmol) and allyltributyltin (198 mg, 0.6 mmol) at room temperature. After
stirred for 3 h (TLC showed the reaction was completed). The suspension
was filtered and washed with CH3CN (3 x 5 mL). The filtrate was
concentrated under reduced pressure to furnish the pure product, 3a
(71mg, 96%). The resulted polymer P5a (320 mg) was stirred in a solution
of HCl (2 M, 15 mL) and Et2O (5 mL) at room temperature for 24 h. Then
filtered and washed with Et2O (3 x 15 mL) to recover P4a. The Et2O layer
was dried and concentrated under reduced pressure to recover Bu3SnCl (180
mg, 92% based on allyltributyltin). 1-(4-Nitrophenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (3b) 9
1H NMR (300MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.19(dd, 2H, J = 1.8, 8.8 Hz), 7.52(d, 2H, J =
8.5 Hz), 5.58-5.72(m, 1H), 5.23-5.17(m, 2H), 4.86(t, 1H, J = 3.6 Hz),
2.61-2.38(m, 2H), 2.24(d, 1H, J = 3.0 Hz); IR (KBr, film): υ 3416, 3078,
2911, 1641, 1604, 1591, 1347, 1055 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported catalyst, last stage for catalyst recovery
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Allylation of Aldehydes and Imines: Promoted by Reusable
Polymer-Supported Sulfonamide of N-Glycine
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Li, Gui-Long; Zhao, Gang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(4), 633-636

