$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (d1) General procedure for the 1,2-addition of
organoboronate esters to aldehydes (3k-3t) A magnetic stirring bar,
organoboronate ester 2 (1.5 mmol), aldehyde 1 (1.0 mmol) and n-undecane
(25 μL, as GC internal standard) are introduced in a 20-mL scintillation
vial with a plastic screwcap. The headspace of the vial is sparged with
argon gas (~1 min), the vial is capped and then introduced inside an
argon atmosphere glovebox. To the vial is added CsF (228 mg, 1.5 mmol)
and an aliquot of a catalyst solution made of either Ni(cod)2, IPr·HCl,
CsF (1:1:2) in PhMe (stirred ~ 24h at room temp. inside the glovebox
before the reaction) or Ni(cod)2, IPr (1:1) in PhMe (stirred ~10 min at
room temp. inside the glovebox before adding to the reaction). An aliquot
of the catalyst solution is added so that the resulting reaction mixture
contains 0.05 mmol Ni(cod)2/IPr and ca. 3 mL PhMe for a 1-mmol scale
reaction. The reaction mixture is then stirred inside the glovebox at
room temperature (~23-30°C) overnight (~12-24h). After the reaction is
completed, the vial is taken out of the glovebox and contents are diluted
with Et2O (~5 mL) and H2O (~3 mL), and stirred for ca. 1h at room
temperature. The organic layer is passed on a short silica plug, eluted
with Et2O and the solvents are evaporated under reduced pressure to
afford the crude secondary alcohol 3.
(E)-1-(2-Methoxyphenyl)-3-phenylprop-2-en-1-ol (3p). Following general
procedure (d1) with 1p (120 μL; 1.0 mmol), 2p (324 mg; 1.5 mmol), CsF
(228 mg, 1.5 mmol), Ni(cod)2/IPr catalyst solution (2 g of a solution
made from Ni(cod)2 (83 mg), IPr·HCl (128 mg), CsF (91 mg) and PhMe (13
g)) and additional PhMe (~1 g). After completion, to the reaction mixture
was added a solution of diethanolamine (1 g) in THF (6 mL) and the
contents were stirred for several hours at room temperature in order to
remove excess residual 2p and facilitate chromatographic separation. The
mixture was filtered on a short silica plug, eluted with Et2O and the
solvents were evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude product was
purified by column chromatography on SiO2 using progressively more polar
9:1 → 7:3 (v/v) hexanes : Et2O to afford 3p as a colorless oil that
slowly solidifies (217 mg, 90%). 1H-NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.35-7.31
(m, 3H), 7.27-7.21 (m, 3H), 7.18 (t, 1H, J = 7.6 Hz), 6.94 (t, 1H, J =
7.6 Hz), 6.87 (d, 1H, J = 7.6 Hz), 6.61 (d, 1H, J = 15.8 Hz), 6.44 (dd,
1H, J = 15.8, 6.2 Hz), 5.54 (t, 1H, J = 6.2 Hz), 3.84 (s, 3H), 2.84 (d,
1H, J = 6.2 Hz); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 137.0, 131.0, 130.0,
128.9, 128.6 (2), 127.6, 126.6 (2), 121.0, 110.9, 71.5, 55.5. HR-MS (EI):
calcd. for C16H16O2 [M]+ 240.1150, found 240.1142.
