$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 18d. To a solution of (S,S) Duthaler-Hafner titanium complex (17.26 g,
28.16 mmol, 1.5 equiv) in Et2O (352 mL) at 0 °C was added dropwise
allylmagnesium chloride (2.0 M in THF, 12.2 mL, 1.3 equiv) over 15 min
and the mixture was maintained for 1.5 h. The mixture was then cooled to
–78 °C. To the mixture was added dropwise a solution of aldehyde 18c
(6.92 g, 18.8 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in Et2O (94 mL) over 15 min and the
mixture was maintained for 4 h. The reaction was quenched with water and
was allowed to warm to ambient temperature and was stirred vigorously for
14 h. The mixture was filtered through celite® and the layers were
separated. The organic phase was washed twice with water and once with
brine. The combined aqueous layers were extracted twice with EtOAc. The
combined organic phases were dried with MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated
in vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography (30% EtOAc/hexanes)
furnished 7.08 g (92%) of diol 18d as a colorless oil: [α]22 D +3.7 (c
1.21, CH3Cl); IR (neat) 3391, 3072, 2931, 1428, 1113; 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.68–7.65 (m, 4H), 7.46–7.39 (m, 6H), 5.77 (ddt, J = 17.3, 10.2,
7.1, 1H), 5.68–5.62 (m, 1H), 5.53 (dd, J = 15.4, 6.4, 1H), 5.13–5.09 (m,
2H), 4.11 (q, J = 6.3, 1H), 3.77 (dq, J = 6.5, 3.8, 1H), 3.66 (dd, J =
10.2, 3.8, 1H), 3.54 (dd, J = 10.2, 6.9, 1H), 2.31–2.21 (m, 4H), 1.98 (s,
br, 2H), 1.08 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 135.8, 135.3, 134.4,
133.31, 133.29, 130.1,128.0, 127.4, 118.4, 71.7, 71.6, 67.5, 42.0, 36.1,
