$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of Hydroxy
DienylSulfoxides. A round-bottomed flask was charged with THF(3.5
mL/mmol) and 2.6 equiv of freshly distilled i-Pr2NH, andcooled to -78 °C.
To the above solution was added 2.5 equiv of n-BuLi and the resulting LDA
solution (ca. 0.3 M) wasstirred at this temperature. After 10 min a
solution of 1 equivof a mixture of dienyl sulfoxides in THF (2
mL/mmol),previously dried over 4 Å sieves, was added dropwise slowly(ca.
8 min/mmol of sulfoxide) to produce a pale yellow solution.After the
solution was stirred for an additional 10 min at -78°C, 5 equiv of
freshly distilled aldehyde was added dropwiseand the resulting colorless
solution was stirred at this temperaturefor 10 min. The reaction mixture
was quenched witha saturated solution of NH4Cl (2 mL/mmol) and H2O (2
mL/mmol), then diluted with EtOAc (3 mL/mmol), and the layerswere
separated. The aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc(3 times, 4
mL/mmol). The combined organic extracts were washed with a saturated
solution of NaCl (4 mL/mmol), driedover MgSO4, and concentrated under
reduced pressure to give a crude product that was purified by column
chromatographywith the appropriate mixture of eluents. 1.5. Synthesis of
(+)-(3R,SS)-(4E)-2-Methyl-4-(p-tolylsulfinyl)hepta-4,6-dien-3-ol, 3d, and
(+)-(3S,SS)-(4E)-2-Methyl-4-(p-tolylsulfinyl)hepta-4,6-dien-3-ol, 4d.
From dienyl sulfoxides 1a,2a (577 mg, 3 mmol), 2.5 equiv of LDA and
isobutyraldehyde (1.36 mL,15 mmol) according to the general procedure, a
36:64 mixture of hydroxy dienyl sulfoxides 3d and 4dwas obtained.
Chromatographic purification (0-40% EtOAc-CH2Cl2), gave 3d (354 mg, 33%)
as a colorless oil and 4d (632 mg, 60%) as a white solid that was
recrystallized from EtOAc-hexane.Racemic material was obtained similarly
on a 30 mmol scale (83%). Data of 3d: Rf = 0.32 (15% EtOAc-CH2Cl2).
[α]20D = +83.2 (c = 1.06). 1H NMR (200 MHz) δ 0.74 (d, 3 H, J = 6.8 Hz),
0.99 (d, 3 H, J = 6.5 Hz), 1.90-2.00 (m, 2 H), 2.37 (s, 3 H), 4.27 (dd, 1
H, J =8.3, 4.7 Hz), 5.47 (dd, 1 H, J = 9.9, 1.6 Hz), 5.59 (dd, 1 H, J =
16.6, 1.6 Hz), 6.70 (ddd, 1 H, J = 16.6,11.2, 9.9 Hz), 6.99 (d, 1 H, J =
11.2 Hz), 7.26 (d, 2 H, J = 8.1 Hz), 7.54 (d, 2 H, J = 8.2 Hz). 13C
NMR(50 MHz) δ 18.4, 19.0, 21.2, 34.0, 74.4, 124.4, 125.2 (2 C), 129.7 (2
C), 130.5, 132.7, 141.2, 141.3, 146.7. IR (CCl4): 3300, 2940, 1585, 1485,
1460, 1170, 1070, 1000, 915, 800 cm-1. MS (EI): 265[M+1]+, 247, 221, 140,
123, 107, 92 (100%), 79, 65, 55, 43. Anal. calcd for C15H20O2S: C, 68.14;
H,7.62; S, 12.13. Found: C, 68.37; H, 7.83; S, 12.37. Data of 4d: mp
(racemic): 73-74 °C. Rf = 0.17 (15% EtOAc-CH2Cl2). [α]20D = +180.7 (c =
1.06).1H NMR (200 MHz) δ 0.71 (d, 3 H, J = 6.8 Hz), 0.93 (d, 3 H, J = 6.5
Hz), 1.75-1.86 (m, 1 H), 2.37(s, 3 H), 2.54 (d, 1 H, J = 4.9 Hz), 3.93
(dd, 1 H, J = 8.3 Hz, 4.7 Hz), 5.40-5.60 (m, 2 H), 6.72-6.93 (m,2 H),
7.26 (d, 2 H, J = 8.6 Hz), 7.53 (d, 2 H, J = 8.2 Hz). 13C NMR (50 MHz) δ
18.8, 19.0, 21.4,34.1, 74.8, 123.9, 126.0 (2 C), 129.9 (2 C), 131.2,
132.1, 139.9, 142.0, 146.5. IR (CCl4): 3300, 2940,1580, 1480, 1455, 1065,
1015, 1000, 910, 800 cm-1. MS (EI): 221, 140, 105, 91, 57, 43
(100%).Anal. calcd for C15H20O2S: C, 68.14; H, 7.62; S, 12.13. Found: C,
68.06; H, 7.48; S, 12.31.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nucleophilic Epoxidation of α'-Hydroxy Dienyl Sulfoxides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fernandez de la Pradilla, Roberto; Manzano, Pilar; Montero, Carlos;
