$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of phenylacetylene (4.0 mL, 36 mmol) in dry tetrahydrofuran
(140 mL) at -78°C was added n-butyllithium (2.5M in hexanes , 12.3 mL,
30.9 mmol) slowly. The solution was stirred for 10 min, then warmed to
0°C. After stirring for 10 mins, the solution was re-cooled to -78°C and
a solution of cyclohex-1-enecarbaldehyde (3.2 mL, 28 mmol) in dry
tetrahydrofuran (209 mL) was added dropwise via addition funnel. After
addition, the cooling bath was removed and the reaction solution was
stirred at room temperature for 3 h. The solution was quenched with
saturated aqueous ammonium chloride (200 mL) and concentrated in vacuo.
Water (150 mL) was added, then the mixture extracted with diethyl ether
(3 x 150 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with brine (100
mL), dried over anhydrous MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The
resulting yellow oil was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
propargylic alcohol S6a (6.3 g, >99%) as a pale yellow oil.
1-cyclohexenyl-3-phenylprop-2-yn-1-ol (S6a). (10:0-8:2 hexanes/ ethyl
acetate, >99%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ7.52-7.47 (m, 2H), 7.40-7.34 (m,
3H), 6.04 (s, 1H), 5.01 (d, J = 5.6 Hz, 1H), 2.40-2.10 (m, 4H), 1.93 (d,
J = 5.6 Hz, 1H), 1.82-1.72 (m, 2H), 1.72-1.63 (m, 2H).
