$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical reaction procedure for the
intramolecular Morita-Baylis-Hillman reactions:
1-(5-hydroxy-1-cyclopentenyl)-1-propanone (3a). 1 To a stirred solution
of 1a (105 mg, 0.75 mmol) in t-BuOH (7.5 mL) was added PPh3 (197 mg, 0.75
mmol) at 40 °C. The mixture was stirred at that temperature for 60 h,
diluted with ethyl acetate, washed with water, dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude
product was purified by flash chromatography to afford 3a (76 mg, 0.54
mmol) in 72% yield. 1-(5-Hydroxy-1-cyclopentenyl)pentanone (3b). 1 Yellow
oil IR (CH2Cl2): ν 3487, 3055, 2933, 2871, 1659, 1619, 1455, 1380, 1055,
982, 739 cm-1 ; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ 0.92 (3H, t, J = 7.4 Hz,
CH3), 1.26-1.41 (2H, m, CH2), 1.56-1.66 (2H, m, CH2), 1.77-1.88 (1H, m,
