$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1-(3-Nitrophenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (1q)11 Following the
Representative Procedure, 3-nitrobenzaldehyde (151 mg, 1.0 mmol),
RuCl3•xH2O (6.2 mg, 0.03 mmol, 0.03 equiv), allyl acetate (130 μL, 1.2
mmol, 1.2 equiv), H2O (27 μL, 1.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv), Et3N (14 μL, 0.1
mmol, 0.1 equiv), hexamethylbenzene (16 mg, 0.1 mmol, internal standard
for NMR analysis) and dioxane (2.5 mL) were combined under 30 psi of CO
at 80 °C for 24 h. Workup and purification by silica gel column
chromatography eluting with hexanes/ethyl acetate (5:1, 450 mL) provided
1q (168 mg, 87%) as a colorless oil. 1-(3-Nitrophenyl)-3-buten-1-ol
(1q)11, yield 168 mg, 87%. Data for 1q: 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) 8.22 (t,
J = 1.5, 1 H, Aryl), 8.11 (ddd, J = 8.0, 2.5, 1.0, 1 H, Aryl), 7.69 (d, J
= 8.0, 1 H, Aryl), 7.51 (t, J = 8.0, 1 H, Aryl), 5.79 (dddd, J = 16.5,
10.0, 8.0, 7.0, 1 H, HC(3)), 5.19-5.15 (m, 2 H, H2C(4)), 4.85 (quint, J =
3.5, 1 H, HC(1)), 2.59- 2.44 (m, 2 H, H2C(2)), 2.38 (d, J = 3.5, 1 H, HO)
13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) 148.2 (C(3')), 145.9 (C(1')), 133.2 (C(3)),
131.9 (C(5')), 129.3 (C(6')), 122.4 (C(2')), 120.8 (C(4')), 119.5 (C(4)),
72.0 (C(1)), 43.8 (C2)). IR (NaCl) 3411 (m), 3077 (w), 2976 (w), 2907
(w), 1641 (m), 1529 (s), 1479 (m), 1436 (m), 1350 (s), 1200 (m), 1093
(m), 1055 (m), 922 (m), 808 (m). HRMS (CI) Calcd. for C10H12NO3,
194.0817; found, 194.0815 TLC Rf 0.29 (hexanes/ethyl acetate, 5:1) [UV,
CAM]
