$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The asymmetric allylation reaction began with formation of the
(S,S)-reagent 4 (R3 = H) by the addition of BBr3 (0.21 mL, 1 M in CH2Cl2)
into a solution of (S,S)-1,2-diamino-1,2-diphenylethane
bis-N,N-toluenefulonamide (109.4 mg, 0.21 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2.3 mL) at 0
°C. This mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 15 minutes, and then warmed to
room temperature and allowed to stir for 60 minutes. The solvent was
removed in vacuo and the resulting yellow solid was redissolved in dry
CH2Cl2 (2 mL) and allowed to stir for 10 minutes. The solvent was again
removed in vacuo and the resulting yellow solid was resuspended in dry
CH2Cl2 (2 mL). This sequence was usually repeated one more time prior to
the introduction of allyltributylstannane (0.090 mL, 0.290 mmol), and the
mixture was then allowed to stir at room temperature overnight (8-9 hrs).
The reaction was then cooled to -78 °C, and a solution of aldehyde 12
(52.9 mg; 0.15 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL) was introduced into the cold
solution. The reaction was stirred at -78 °C for 2 hours and was then
quenched at that temperature by the dropwise addition of aqueous pH 7
buffer (1 mL). The quenched reaction mixture was allowed to warm to room
temperature and a solution of saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (5 mL) was added
with additional stirring for 10 min. The phases were separated and the
aqueous phase was extracted three times with CH2Cl2. The combined organic
phases were dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuo. The resulting
residue was washed with hexanes and filtered to remove the insoluble
sulfonamide ligand. The solution of hexanes was concentrated in vacuo to
yield a crude material which was purified by flash column chromatography
on silica gel (EtOAc in hexanes) affording alcohol 19.
(4S,7S,E)-7-((tert-Butyldiphenylsilyl)oxy)-5-methylocta-1,5-dien-4-ol
(19), yield 44.6 mg, 0.113 mmol, 75% (99:1). Rf = 0.29 (90:10
hexanes:EtOAc); [α]D22 -33.4 (c 0.45, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
(ppm): 7.68 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 4H), 7.44 - 7.33 (m, 6H), 5.66 (ddt, J =
17.1, 10.2, 7.3 Hz, 1H), 5.41 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 5.06 (d, J = 15.6 Hz,
1H), 5.03 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 4.60 - 4.55 (m, 1H), 3.82 (t, J = 6.8 Hz,
1H), 2.18 (td, J = 7.1, 1.4 Hz, 3H), 1.28 (s, 1H), 1.19, 1.05 (s, 9H);
13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 136.0, 135.2, 134.9, 134.6, 131.7,
129.7, 127.7, 127.5, 117.5, 76.2, 66.6, 39.4, 27.1, 24.3, 19.3, 11.6;
HRMS-ESI (calc. for C25H34O2Si [M+Na]+) 417.2226, found 417.2221.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, agent dependent stereochemistry, in-situ generated
reactant in stage 2, buffered solution used in stage 4
