$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The asymmetric allylation reaction began with the addition of BBr3 (0.19
mL, 1 M in CH2Cl2) into a solution of
(R,R)-1,2-diamino-1,2-diphenylethane-N,N-sulfonamide (0.100 g; 0.192
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2 mL) at 0 °C. This mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 15
minutes, and then warmed to room temperature and allowed to stir for 60
minutes. The solvent was removed in vacuo and the resulting yellow solid
was redissolved in dry CH2Cl2 (2 mL) and allowed to stir for 10 minutes.
The solvent was again removed in vacuo and the resulting yellow solid was
resuspended in dry CH2Cl2 (2 mL). This sequence was usually repeated one
more time prior to the introduction of allyltributylstannane (0.090 mL,
0.290 mmol), and the mixture was then allowed to stir at room temperature
overnight (8-9 hrs). The reaction was then cooled to -78 °C, and a
solution of aldehyde 10 (54.3 mg; 0.148 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL) was
introduced into the cold solution. The reaction was stirred at -78 °C for
2 hours and was then quenched at that temperature by the dropwise
addition of aqueous pH 7 buffer (1 mL). The quenched reaction mixture was
allowed to warm to room temperature and a solution of saturated aqueous
NaHCO3 (5 mL) was added with additional stirring for 10 min. The phases
were separated and the aqueous phase was extracted three times with
CH2Cl2. The combined organic phases were dried over Na2SO4 and
concentrated in vacuo. The resulting residue was washed with hexanes and
filtered to remove the insoluble sulfonamide ligand. The solution of
hexanes was concentrated in vacuo to yield a crude material which was
purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc in hexanes)
affording alcohol 17.
(4R,7S,E)-8-((tert-Butyldiphenylsilyl)oxy)-5,7-dimethylocta-1,5-dien-4-ol
(17), yield 44.9 mg, 0.11 mmol, 73% (99:1). Rf = 0.23 (90:10
hexanes:EtOAc); [α]D22 +20.5 (c 0.52, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
(ppm): 7.66 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 4H), 7.43 - 7.34 (m, 6H), 5.75 (ddt, J =
16.9, 10.1, 7.2 Hz, 1H), 5.20 (ddd, J = 10.6, 5.1, 3.6 Hz, 1H), 5.10 (d,
J = 17.5 Hz, 1H), 5.06 (d, J = 10.3 Hz, 1H), 4.02 - 3.99 (m, 1H), 3.50 -
3.43 (m, 2H), 2.66 - 2.59 (m, 1H), 2.31 - 2.23 (m, 2H), 1.59 (s, 3H),
1.26 (s, 1H), 1.05 (s, 9H), 0.99 (t, J = 14.4, 7.2 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (125
MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 137.0, 135.8, 135.0, 134.1, 129.7, 129.5, 127.7,
117.7, 117.7, 76.6, 68.6, 40.1, 35.2, 27.0, 19.4, 17.4, 12.1; HRMS-ESI
(calc. for C26H36O2Si [M+Na]+) 431.2382, found 431.2371.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, agent dependent stereochemistry, in-situ generated
reactant in stage 2, buffered solution used in stage 4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereocontrol in Asymmetric SE' Reactions of γ-Substituted
α,β-Unsaturated Aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Williams, David R.; Atwater, Bruce A.; Bawel, Seth A.; Ke, Pucheng;
Gutierrez, Osvaldo; Tantillo, Dean J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(2), 468-471

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME166 STEP1
$RXN



