$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Freshly distilled CH2Cl2 (5 mL) was added and
evaporated under vauum as above. Freshly distilled CH2Cl2 (3 mL) was
added and the homogeneous solution of (R,R)-4c was cooled to -78 °C, and
treated dropwise with a mixture of methyl allenoate (1, R1 = Me, 0.1 g,
1.02 mmol) and i-Pr2NEt (0.35 mL, 0.26 g, 2.01 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL).
The reaction mixture was allowed to proceed at -78 °C. After stirring for
20 min at -78 °C, pre-cooled hydrocinnamaldehyde (0.13 mL, 0.133 g, 1.0
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL) was added via cannular along the wall of the flask
while keeping the temperature below -78 °C. The reaction was allowed to
proceed for 2 h at -78 °C, and then quenched by addition of aqueous
buffer solution (pH 7, 7 mL) followed by CH2Cl2 (ca 10 mL) to dissolve
white precipitate (bis-sulfonamide). The aqueous layer was extracted with
CH2Cl2 (ca 10 mL x 2). The combined organic extracts were washed with
brine (1x), dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered, evaporated, and taken
up ether (ca 20 mL). The solution was cooled to 0 °C for 20 min to
complete precipitation of
(+)-(1R,2R)-1,2-diphenyl-1,2-bis-p-toluenesulfonylamide by filtration
through a sintered glass funnel, the filtrate was concentrated under
reduced pressure to give the crude product as fairly pure form. Final
purification was effected by SiO2 chromatography (Hexanes:EtOAc = 85:15).
(-)-(2S)-Methyl 2-(hydroxy(phenyl)methyl)buta-2,3-dienoate (2g) Compound
2g was obtained in 80% yield according to the above procedure for 2a as a
pale yellow liquid. Enantiomeric excess 95%. Rf 0.26 (5:1 Hexane/EtOAc);
[α]D 20-17.56 (c 1.0, CHCl3); IR (neat) 3521, 3062, 2988, 2951, 1964,
1712, 1437, 1270, 1029, 854, 700 cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.51 (d,
J =J = 6.3Hz, 1H), 3.73 (s, 3H), 5.56 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 1H), 5.56 (d, J =
6.3 Hz, 1H), 7.25-7.39 (m, 5H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 52.6, 71.9,
81.4, 103.8, 126.5, 128.0, 128.4, 141.5, 167.3, 213.3; MS (ESI) m/z 205.2
(M+1); Anal. Calcd for C12H12O3: C, 70.57; H, 5.92; O, 23.50. Found: C,
70.29; H, 6.07; HPLC analysis: Daicel Chiralcel OD-H, Hexane/i-PrOH =
24/1, flow rate = 1.5 ml/min, retention time: tR(major) = 13.2 min,
tR(minor) = 15.3 min.
