$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 13 To a flame-dried roundbottom flask containing 11
(500mg, 1.37 mmol) neat at 0°C is added samarium diiodide as a 0.1 M
solution in tetrahydrofuran (34 mL, 3.4 mmol). After 10 minutes
Z-2-bromo-2-pentenal (271 mg, 1.64 mmol) is added as a solution in
tetrahydrofuran (2 mL) and the solution is observed to change from a deep
Prussian blue to a yellow-brown suspension. Acetaldehyde (1.3 mL, 11
mmol) is immediately added and the solution is stirred for 4 hours and
maintained at 0°C. Aqueous saturated ammonium chloride (50 mL) is added
at 0°C and allowed to warm to room temperature. The aqueous phase is
extracted thrice with diethyl ether (50 mL). Combined organic phases are
concentrated, resuspended in methanol (10 mL), and stirred vigorously in
the presence of potassium carbonate (1.52g, 11.0 mmol) for 6 hours. The
resulting slurry is diluted with diethyl ether (100 mL) and washed twice
with saturated brine (50 mL). The aqueous phase is NOT neutralized.
Combined organic phases are dried over sodium sulfate, concentrated under
reduced pressure, and the resulting residue is purified by flash column
chromatography (20% ethyl acetate/hexanes) to afford 13 (590 mg, 96%) as
a pale yellow oil. 13, yield 590 mg, 96% 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) 6.12 (td,
J = 7, 1 Hz, 1H), 5.50 (td, J = 7.5, 0.7 Hz, 1H) 4.47 (d, J = 1.4 Hz,
2H), 4.47-4.39 (m, 2H), 3.72 (d, J = 5.9 Hz, 1H), 3.68 (d, J = 6.8 Hz,
1H), 2.23 (app. quin., J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 2.17-1.99 (m, 4H), 1.19-1.05 (m,
21H), 1.02 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 3H), 0.99 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3) δ 136.9, 131.0, 130.4, 129.6, 73.9, 74.1, 60.5, 39.6, 24.2,
20.8, 18.0, 14.1, 12.9, 11.7; IR (thin film, NaCl) 3402 (m), 2963 (s),
2943 (s), 2891 (m), 2867 (s), 1656 (w), 1462 (m), 1384 (w), 1324 (w),
