$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7-(4-Methoxybenzyloxy)hepta-1,5-dien-4-ol (10). To a cooled (-78 °C)
solution of (+)-Ipc2BOMe (8.22 g, 26.0 mmol) in Et2O (80 mL) were added
allylmagnesium bromide (1.0 M in Et2O, 26.0 mL, 26.0 mmol) dropwise over
15 min. The resulting solution was allowed to warm to room temperature
and stirred for 1 h. The mixture was recooled to -78 °C, then a solution
of enal 9 (2.68 g, 13.0 mmol) in Et2O (50.0 mL) was added dropwise over
30 min. After being stirred for 2 h at the same temperature, the
resulting solution was allowed to warm to -40 °C, and the reaction was
quenched with 3 M aqueous NaOH (91.0 mL), 10% aqueous H2O2 (77.0 mL), and
MeOH (77.0 mL). The resulting mixture was warmed to room temperature,
stirred for 10.5 h, and then extracted with Et2O (100 mL×3). The combined
organic layers were dried over MgSO4 and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The residue was purified by silica gel column chromatography
(EtOAc/Hexane = 1/4). Allylalcohol 10 (2.86 g, 11.5 mmol, 89%) as a
colorless oil. 10: [α]30 D +6.7 (c 1.0, CHCl3); IR (neat): 3421 cm-1;
1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.26 (2H, d, J = 8.5 Hz), 6.87 (2H, d, J = 8.5
Hz), 5.74-5.86 (3H, m), 5.17-5.15 (2H, m), 4.45 (2H, s), 4.20 (1H, dt, J
= 5.1, 7.1 Hz), 4.00 (2H, d, J = 4.4 Hz), 3.80 (3H, s), 2.24-2.39 (2H,
m), 1.73 (1H, brs); 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 159.1, 134.8, 134.0,
130.2, 129.3, 127.4, 118.3, 113.7, 71.9, 71.0, 69.7, 55.3, 41.8; LR-MS
(EI) m/z 248 (M+), 121 (100%); HR-MS (EI) calcd. for C15H20O3 (M+)
248.1412, found 248.1397; TLC (EtOAc/Hexane = 1/2) Rf 0.31.
