$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reaction of Silane 1 with Aldehydes 3. General
Procedure. Method A. AcOLi (17 mg, 0.25 mmol) was added to a solution of
aldehyde 3 (0.5 mmol) and silane 1 (149 mg, 1.0 mmol) in dry THF (1 mL)
at 0 °C, and the mixture was stirred for 18 h at room temperature. For
the workup, the volatile components were evaporated under vacuum in a
bath not exceeding 25 °C, and the residue was dissolved in acetonitrile
(1 mL), treated with CF3CO2H (77 μL, 1.0 mmol) and KHF2 (47 mg, 0.6
mmol), and stirred for 30 min. The mixture was diluted with water (5 mL)
and extracted with tert-butyl methyl ether (3 × 3 mL). The organic phase
was dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated, and the residue was purified by
chromatography. (4E)-2,2-Difluoro-3-hydroxy-5-phenylpent-4-enenitrile
(5i). Method A, 75 mg, 72% yield. Colorless oil. Chromatography was
performed at -30 °C; Rf 0.29 (hexanes/EtOAc 5:1); 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 2.80-2.98 (br, 1H), 4.68 (q, 1H, J = 7.4), 6.19 (dd, 1H, J = 15.8,
7.4), 6.95 (d, 1H, J = 15.8), 7.34-7.51 (m, 5H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 73.7 (t, J = 26.8), 110.7 (t, J = 249.6), 111.2 (t, J = 44.3), 119.1
(dd, J = 3.5, 1.7), 127.0, 128.8, 129.1, 135.0, 137.8; 19F NMR (282 MHz,
CDCl3) δ -100.9 (dd, 1F, J = 290.3, 7.4), -103.7 (dd, 1F, J = 290.3,
7.4). Calcd for C11H9F2NO (209.19): C, 63.16; H, 4.34; N, 6.70. Found: C,
63.08; H, 4.45; N, 6.81.
