$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the reaction of Grignard
reagents with aldehydes: The corresponding aldehyde (1 mmol) was
dissolved in 5 mL of anhydrous THF at -78 °C. To this solution 1.2 mmol
of Grignard reagent was added dropwise and the mixture was stirred for 3
h at -78 °C. After this time, the reaction was quenched with saturated
NH4Cl (5 mL) and extracted with EtOAc (3× 10 mL). The organic layer was
washed with brine (10 mL), dried with MgSO4, filtered and concentrated.
The crude product was purified and/or separated by column chromatography
using hexane/EtOAc mixtures as eluents.
1-(2-Trimethylsilylethynylphenyl)prop-2-en-1-ol, 6a; 2.0 g (90%);
colorless oil. 1H NMR δ 0.26 (s, 9H), 2.54 (s, 1H), 5.17 (d, 1H, J= 10.4
Hz), 5.37 (d, 1H, J= 17.0 Hz), 5.64 (d, 1H, J= 5.5 Hz), 6.03 (ddd, 1H,
J1= 17.0 Hz, J2= 9.9 Hz, J3= 5.5 Hz), 7.21 (t, 1H, J= 8.8 Hz), 7.33 (t,
1H, J= 8.8 Hz), 7.45 (d, 2H, J= 7.7 Hz). 13C-NMR δ 144.8, 139.0, 132.6,
129.0, 127.2, 125.8, 120.7, 114.9, 102.8, 99.8, 73.1,-0.1 . IR (neat) ν
3350, 2950, 2140 cm-1 . Anal. Calc. for C14H18OSi: C, 72.99; H, 7.88.
Found: C, 72.92; H, 7.70.
