$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative procedure for catalytic
reductive aldol reaction of α,β-unsaturated aldehydes (Table 1): A 10 mL
flame-dried round bottom flask was charged with 16.5 mg of
[(cod)Rh(R)-binap]BF4 (0.018 mmol), and 500 μL of dichloroethane. The
resulting solution was stirred at room temperature for approximately one
minute or until the rhodium complex was fully dissolved. After the
complex was fully dissolved, 62 μL of diethylmethylsilane (0.428 mmol)
was added to the mixture and the reaction vessel stirred for 30 minutes.
Next, 250 μL of dichloroethane followed by 50 μL of phenyl acrylate
(0.357 mmol) and 172 μL 2-methyl-2-butenal (1.78 mmol ) was added to the
solution. The vessel was then sealed and allowed to stir for 24 hours,
after which time 0.5 equivalents of diethylmethylsilane (0.1785 mmol) was
added and the reaction was stirred an additional 24 h . Solvent was then
evaporated from the reaction and 1 mL each of THF, MeOH, and 4N HCl were
added. This mixture was stirred at room temperature for an additional 45
minutes. Ethyl acetate was then used to extract the product (3 x 25 mL).
The combined organic layers were washed with a saturated aqueous sodium
bicarbonate solution (2 x 20 mL), dried over Na2SO4, and filtered. The
solvent was removed by rotary evaporation to yield crude product which
was purified via flash chromatography (16:1, 14:1 then 13:1 hexanes:ethyl
acetate). (2R,3R)-3-hydroxy-2,5-dimethyl-hex-4-ene-onic acid phenyl
ester. IR (KBr) 3450 (br, s) 2980 (m), 1780 (s) 1490 (m), 1200 (s) cm-1;
1H NMR: δ 7.5-7.01 (5H, m, aromatic), 5.35 (br d, J= 8.0 Hz, vinylic CH)
4.71 (1H, m, CHOH), 2.75 (1H, dq, J=6.7, 6.8 Hz, CH3CH), 2.26 (1H, d,
J=4.6 Hz, OH), 1.78 (3H, s, vinyl CH 3), 1.74 (3H, s, vinyl CH 3), 0.88
(3H, d, J=7.2 Hz, CHCH 3); 13C NMR: δ 174.0, 151.0, 137.6, 129.8, 126.3,
124.8, 121.9, 70.1,46.3, 26.3,18.8,12.8. HRMS Calc'd for C14H19O3 [M+H]+:
235.1334, Found: 235.1342.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, addnl. silane added after 24 h in stage 2, syn ee 83%,
aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Investigation of the Rh-Catalyzed Asymmetric Reductive Aldol Reaction.
Expanded Scope Based on Reaction Analysis
