$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM a) 1-(3,5-Dimethoxy-phenyl)-but-3-en-1-ol : Allyl magnesium bromide
(28.89 mL, 28.89 mmol, 1.2 eq, 1M solution in Et2O) was added to a
solution of (+)-IPC2BOMe (9.14 9, 28.89 mmol, 1.2 eq) and Et2O (60.2 mL)
at -78 °C in a flame dried flask under N2(g). The resulting cloudy, white
solution was warmed to rt for 1 h and then returned to -78 °C, at which
point the aldehyde (4.0 g, 24. 07 mmol, 1.0 eq) was added dropwise in
Et2O (5 mL). The reaction was stirred for 2 h at -78 °C and then warmed
to rt for 1 h. Upon completion, the flask was cooled to 0 °C and NaOH
(21.4 mL) and H2O2 (11.6 mL) were added dropwise via addition funnel. To
complete to oxidation process, the reaction was refluxed for 45 min. The
layers were separated and the organic layer was dried with MgSO4,
filtered and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by flash column chromatography (5% EtOAc, /Hexanes) to provide
as an oil, yield 3.75 g, 75%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.53 (s, 1H),
6.52 (s, 1H), 6.38 (t, 1H, J = 2.3 Hz), 5.85- 5.94 (m, 1H), 5.17 (dd, 1H,
J = 1.8, 15.8 Hz), 5.15 (dd, 1H, J = 1.9, 9.1 Hz), 4.67 (dd, 1H, J = 4.9,
7.8 Hz), 3.80 (s, 6H), 2.44- 2.55 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
160.78, 146.48, 134.38, 118.38, 103.64, 99.36, 73. 27, 55.29, 43.68; [α]D
+31.70 (c 1.1, CHCl3); IR (thin film) 3426, 3000, 2937, 2838, 1598, 1463,
1429, 1349, 1295, 1204, 1155, 1059, 920 cm-1; HRMS (EI) calculated for
C12H17O3 [M+H+] = 209.1172, found 209.1173 ± 0.4 ppm.
