$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure II: Aldol Addition of (Z)-5:
(1R,2R,4S)-5-tert-Butyldimethylsilyloxy-2,4-dimethyl-1-hydroxy-1-phenyl-3-pentanone
(syn,syn-16a) Trichlorosilyl enol ether (Z)-5 (364 mg, 1.00 mmol) was
added to a solution of (R,R)-1a (37 mg, 0.10 mmol, 0.10 equiv) in 1.00 mL
of CH2Cl2. The reaction mixture was cooled to -78°C using an acetone/CO2
bath, and PhCHO (102 mL, 1.00 mmol, 1 equiv) was added by syringe. After
stirring for 6 h, the reaction mixture was quenched by pouring into a
vigorously stirred solution of cold, sat. aq. NaHCO3 solution. The
resulting slurry was stirred for 1 h and was filtered through Celite. The
layers were separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with 10 mL of
CH2Cl2. The organic phases were combined, washed with 2 mL of brine and
were dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated. The crude product was
purified by column chromatography (pentane/ether, 3/1, SiO2) to afford
241 mg (0.72 mmol, 72%) of 16a as a clear, viscous oil.
(2S,4R,5R)-1-Triisopropylsilyloxy-2,4-dimethyl-5-hydroxy-7-phenyl-6-hepten-3-one
(syn,syn-17c)9 Following General Procedure II from (Z)-6 (872 mg, 2.00
mmol), cinnamaldehyde (252 mL, 2.00 mmol, 1.0 equiv), (R,R)-1a (74 mg,
0.20 mmol, 0.1 equiv) and TBAI (148 mg, 0.40 mmol, 0.2 equiv) in 2 mL of
CH2Cl2 for 10 h, was obtained 713 mg (1.76 mmol, 88%) of 17c as a clear,
colorless, viscous oil after column chromatography (pentane/ether, 3/1,
SiO2). 1H NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3) 7.38 (d, J = 7.1, 2 H, HC(13)); 7.31 (t,
J = 7.5, 2 H, HC(14)); 7.24 (t, J = 7.4, 1 H, HC(15)); 6.64 (dd, J =
15.8, 0.9, 1 H, HC(7)); 6.13 (dd, J = 15.8, 5.6, 1 H, HC(6)); 4.75 (m, 1
H, HC(5)); 3.88-3.70 (ABX, 2 H, H2C(1)); 3.30 (d, J = 2.9, 1 H, HO); 3.09
(sext, J = 5.4, 1 H, HC(2)); 2.95 (qd, J = 7.3, 2.7, 1 H, HC(4)); 1.17
(d, J =7.4, 3 H, H3C(11)); 1.11 - 1.02 (m, 24 H, H3C(9), H3C(10), HC(8))
13C NMR: (126 MHz, CDCl3) 219.39 (C(3)); 137.07 (C(12)); 130.91 (C(6));
129.19 (C(7)); 128.76 (C(14)); 127.75 (C(15)); 126.64 (C(13)); 71.48
(C(1)); 67.19 (C(5)); 51.51 (C(4)); 47.61 (C(2)); 18.15 (C(9)); 13.40
(C(10)); 12.01 (C(8)); 9.64 (C(11)) IR: (neat) 3436 (br, m); 3061 (w);
3027 (w); 2943 (s); 2892 (m); 2867 (m); 1703 (m); 1600 (w); 1495(w); 1462
(m); 1384 (w); 1368 (w); 1249 (w); 1102 (m); 1069 (m) MS: (FI) 406.2 (9);
405.2 (34); 404.2 (M+, 100); 335.2 (9); 272.1 (8); 229.1 (24); 132.0 (48)
Opt. Rot.: [α]D 24 + 20.0 (c = 0.73, CH2Cl2) [α]D 24 - 47.8 (c = 0.73,
EtOH) TLC: Rf 0.12 (pentane/ether, 3/1) [silica gel, short UV] SFC: tR
3.348 min (OD, 150 bar, 3 mL/min, 7% MeOH) Analysis: C24H40O3Si (404.66)
Calcd: C, 71.23; H, 9.96% Found: C, 71.27; H, 10.08%
