(1R,2R,4S)-5-tert-Butyldimethylsilyloxy-2,4-dimethyl-1-hydroxy-1-phenyl-3-pentanone
(syn,syn-16a) Trichlorosilyl enol ether (Z)-5 (364 mg, 1.00 mmol) was
added to a solution of (R,R)-1a (37 mg, 0.10 mmol, 0.10 equiv) in 1.00 mL
of CH2Cl2. The reaction mixture was cooled to -78°C using an acetone/CO2
bath, and PhCHO (102 mL, 1.00 mmol, 1 equiv) was added by syringe. After
stirring for 6 h, the reaction mixture was quenched by pouring into a
vigorously stirred solution of cold, sat. aq. NaHCO3 solution. The
resulting slurry was stirred for 1 h and was filtered through Celite. The
layers were separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with 10 mL of
CH2Cl2. The organic phases were combined, washed with 2 mL of brine and
were dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated. The crude product was
purified by column chromatography (pentane/ether, 3/1, SiO2) to afford
241 mg (0.72 mmol, 72%) of 16a as a clear, viscous oil.
(2S,4S,5S)-1-Triisopropylsilyloxy-2,4-dimethyl-5-hydroxy-7-phenyl-6-hepten-3-one
Following General Procedure II from (Z)-6 (436 mg, 1.00 mmol),
cinnamaldehyde (126 mL, 1.00 mmol, 1.0 equiv), (S,S)-1a (37 mg, 0.10
mmol, 0.1 equiv) and TBAI (73.9 mg, 0.20 mmol, 0.2 equiv) in 1 mL of
CH2Cl2 for 10 h, was obtained 303 mg (0.75 mmol, 75%) of 17c as a clear,
colorless, viscous oil after column chromatography (pentane/ether, 3/1,
SiO2). 1H NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3) 7.38 (d, J = 7.6, 2 H, HC(13)); 7.31 (t,
J = 7.6, 2 H, HC(14)); 7.24 (t, J = 7.8, 1 H, HC(15)); 6.65 (d, J = 16.1,
1 H, HC(7)); 6.13 (dd, J = 15.8, 5.8, 1 H, HC(6)); 4.64 (br m, 1 H,
HC(5)); 3.94-3.65 (ABX, 2 H, H2C(1)); 3.03 (sext, J = 5.4, 1 H, HC(2));
2.99 (d, J = 2.9, 1 H, HO); 2.92 (qd, J = 7.3, 3.6, 1 H, HC(4)); 1.18 (d,
J =6.5, 3 H, H3C(11)); 1.16 - 1.04 (m, 24 H, H3C(9), H3C(10), HC(8)) 13C
NMR: (101 MHz, CDCl3) 218.13 (C(3)); 137.07 (C(12)); 130.92 (C(6));
129.14 (C(7)); 128.54 (C(14)); 127.60 (C(15)); 126.43 (C(13)); 72.33
(C(1)); 65.85 (C(5)); 50.52 (C(4)); 48.14 (C(2)); 17.94 (C(9)); 15.27
(C(10)); 11.84 (C(8)); 9.91 (C(11)) IR: (neat) 3430 (br, m); 3083 (w);
3061 (w); 3027 (w); 2943 (s); 2892 (s); 2726 (w); 1706 (s); 1627 (w);
1600 (w); 1578 (w); 1495(m); 1462 (s); 1383 (m); 1368 (m); 1250 (m); 1203
(w); 1104 (s); 1068 (s) MS: (FI) 405.2 (12); 404.2 (M+, 34); 287.1 (11);
273.1 (15); 269.1 (15); 261.1 (69); 245.1 (30); 229.1 (100); 217.0 (83);
131.9 (17); 106.0 (28) Opt. Rot.: [α]D 24 + 42.1 (c = 1.35, CH2Cl2) [α]D
24 + 109.0 (c = 1.25, EtOH) TLC: Rf 0.23 (pentane/ether, 3/1) [silica
gel, short UV] SFC: tR 6.630 min (OD, 150 bar, 3 mL/min, 7% MeOH)
Analysis: C24H40O3Si (404.66) Calcd: C, 71.23; H, 9.96% Found: C, 71.30;
H, 9.79%
