$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1-(2,4,6-Trimethylphenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (1j)9 Following the
Representative Procedure, 2,4,6-trimethylbenzaldehyde (148 mg, 1.0 mmol),
RuCl3•xH2O (6.2 mg, 0.03 mmol, 0.03 equiv), allyl acetate (130 μL, 1.2
mmol, 1.2 equiv), H2O (27 μL, 1.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv), Et3N (14 μL, 0.1
mmol, 0.1 equiv), hexamethylbenzene (16 mg, 0.1 mmol, internal standard
for NMR analysis) and dioxane (2.5 mL) were combined under 30 psi of CO
at 80 °C for 24 h. Workup and purification by silica gel column
chromatography eluting with pentane/MTBE (10:1, 100 mL; 4:1, 200 mL)
provided 1j (149 mg, 78%) as a colorless oil.
1-(2,4,6-Trimethylphenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (1j)9, yield 149 mg, 78%. Data for
1j: 1H NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3) 6.82 (s, 2 H, Aryl), 5.84 (dddd, J = 16.8,
10.2, 7.9, 6.3, 1 H, HC(3)), 5.18 (d, J = 16.8, 1 H, HaC(4)), 5.17 (ddd,
J = 9.0, 5.1, 1.3, 1 H, HC(1)), 5.12 (d, J = 10.2, 1H, HbC(4)), 2.71
(ddd, J = 14.1, 9.0, 6.3, 1 H, HaC(2)), 2.49 (ddd, J = 14.1, 7.9, 5.1, 1
H, HbC(2)), 2.41 (s, 6 H, H3C(7') & H3C(9')), 2.25 (s, 3 H, H3C(8')),
1.87 (d, J = 1.3, 1 H, HO). 13C NMR: (125 MHz, CDCl3) 136.6 (C(4')),
136.0 (C(1')), 135.2 (C(3)), 130.1 (C(2', 3', 5', 6')), 117.7 (C(4)),
70.7 (C(1)), 40.3 (C(2)), 20.7 (C(7', 8', 9')) IR: (NaCl) 3521 (m), 3390
(s), 3066 (m), 2920 (s), 2862 (m), 1639 (m), 1611 (m), 1446 (s), 1376
(m), 1306 (m), 1045 (s) HRMS: (ESI) Calcd. for C13H18ONa, 213.1255;
found, 213.1261 TLC: Rf 0.32 (hexanes/MTBE, 4:1) [UV, CAM]
