$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Catalytic
Enantioselective Alkylation of Aldehydes Using Alkylboron Reagents. The
stock solution of alkylboron reagents 3 (0.75 M) was prepared by
treatment of alkenes 2 (3.3 equiv) with BH3·SMe2 (2 M in THF) in THF at 0
°C for 1 h and then at room temperature for 14 h. To a mixture of 3 (1
mL, 0.75 mmol), (R)-DPP-H8-BINOL (13 mg, 0.025 mmol), and titanium
tetraisopropoxide (0.44 mL, 1.5 mmol), heated under reflux, was added a
THF (0.7 mL) solution of aldehydes 1 (0.5 mmol) slowly by using a syringe
pump over 4 h. The resulting solution was refluxed for an additional
hour. Two procedures were used for workup. In procedure A, water (0.75
mL) and NaBO3.4H2O5 (520 mg, 3.34 mmol) were added successively at room
temperature and the resulting mixture was heated under reflux for 2 h.
The reaction mixture was quenched by the addition of aqueous 1 N HCl and
extracted three times with ethyl acetate. The organic layers were washed
with aqueous 5% NaHCO3 and brine, dried (Na2SO4), and concentrated in
vacuo. In procedure B, the reaction mixture was quenched by the addition
of aqueous 1 N HCl and extracted three times with ethyl acetate. The
organic layers were washed successively with aqueous 5% NaHCO3 and brine,
dried (Na2SO4), and concentrated in vacuo. To a solution of the residue
in THF (4 mL) and ethanol (1 mL) at room temperature was added aqueous
30% H2O2 (1 mL) and aqueous 6 N NaOH (1 mL). The resulting mixture was
heated under reflux for 1 h. After dilution with water, it was extracted
three times with ethyl acetate. The organic layers were washed with
aqueous Na2S2O4 and brine, dried (Na2SO4), and concentrated in vacuo.
Procedure B was not appropriate in the reaction with boron reagents 3j-l
bearing base sensitive functional groups. The residue was purified by
flash chromatography on silica gel, eluting with ethyl acetate/toluene or
ethyl acetate/hexane. Alkylation products 4. The ee values of 4 were
determined by HPLC analysis using a chiral column.
(R)-1-Naphthalen-1-ylheptan-1-ol (4ac). (94% ee).
(R)-1-Cyclohex-1-enyl-4-phenylbutan-1-ol (4jd). (94% ee).
Enantioselectivity was determined by HPLC analysis using a Chiralcel OD-H
column, 1 mL/min, 4% i-PrOH in hexane; The absolute stereochemistry was
assumed by analogy. [α]D 25 -5.7 (c 0.7, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 1.50-1.72 (9H, m), 1.85 (1H, m), 2.00-2.1 (3H, m), 2.64 (2H, m), 3.98
(1H, t, J = 6.5 Hz), 5.64 (1H, br s), 7.18 (3H, m), 7.28 (2H, m); 13C NMR
(125.8 MHz, CDCl3) δ 22.6 (2C), 23.2, 24.9, 27.6, 34.2, 35.8, 76.5,
123.3, 125.6, 128.2, 128.4, 139.8, 142.4; HRMS (FAB) calcd for C16H22O
230.1671, found 230.1675. retention times: 11.0 min (major R-enantiomer)
and 14.6 min (minor S-enantiomer).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective Alkylation of Aldehydes Using Functionalized Alkylboron
Reagents Catalyzed by a Chiral Titanium Complex
