$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure VI: Aldol Addition of 23:
(+)-(2S,4R,5S)-5-Hydroxy-4-methyl-5-phenyl-
2-[((dimethyl)-(1,1-dimethylethyl)silyl)oxy]-3-pentanone (41a)9 Silyl
enol ether (Z)-14 (273 mg, 1.0 mmol) was added quickly to a stirred
suspension of silicon tetrachloride (230 μL, 2.0 mmol, 2.0 equiv) and
mercuric acetate (3.2 mg, 0.01 mmol, 0.01 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL) at
room temperature. After addition, the mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 18 h, then the volatile components were removed under
reduced pressure (0.1 mmHg) to give a cloudy oil. A solution of (R,R)-1
(18 mg, 0.05 mmol, 0.05 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (2.0 mL) was then added via
cannula and the mixture was cooled to -78 °C. Benzaldehyde (102 μL, 1.0
mmol) was then added dropwise via syringe and the reaction mixture was
allowed to stir at -78 °C for 10 h. The reaction mixture was then poured
into a rapidly stirring sat. aq. NaHCO3 solution (30 mL) submerged in an
ice bath and was allowed to stir at room temperature for 6 h. The
heterogeneous mixture was then filtered through Celite, the organic phase
was separated and the aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 X 15
mL). The organic extracts were combined, dried over Na2SO4, filtered and
concentrated to give a crude oil. Purification by column chromatography
(silica gel, pentane/Et2O, 6/1) afforded 284 mg (88%) of 41a10 as a
clear, colorless oil. The diastereomeric ratio was determined to be
(syn,syn)-41a/minor isomers, 95/5 by SFC analysis.
(-)-(2S,4R,5S)-(E)-5-Hydroxy-4-methyl-7-phenyl-2-[((dimethyl)-(1,1-dimethylethyl)-
silyl)oxy]-6-hepten-3-one (41c), yield 81%. 1H NMR: (CDCl3, 500 MHz)
7.40-7.22 (m, 5 H, 2 X H(C2''), 2 X HC(3''), HC(4'')); 6.66 (dd, J =
15.9, 1.5, 1 H, HC(7)); 6.14 (dd, J = 16.1, 5.9, 1 H, HC(6)); 4.61 (m, 1
H, HC(5)); 4.25 (q, J = 6.9, 1 H, HC(2)); 3.31 (dq, J = 7.1, 3.4, 1 H,
HC(4)); 3.02, (d, J = 2.8, 1 H, OH); 1.35 (d, J = 6.9, 3 H, H3C(1)); 1.19
(d, J = 7.1, 3 H, H3C(1')); 0.93 (s, 9 H, H3C(3''')); 0.10 (d, J = 1.5, 6
H, H3C(1''')) 13C NMR: (CDCl3, 125 MHz) 218.2 (C(3)); 136.7 (C(1''));
131.0 (C(3'')); 129.0 (C(4'')); 128.6 (C(6)); 127.6 (C(7)); 126.5
(C(4'')); 74.6 (C(2)); 71.9 (C(5)); 45.1 (C(4)); 25.7 (C(3''')); 21.2
(C(1)); 18.0 (C(8)); 10.8 (C(1')); -4.6 (C(1''')); -5.0 (C(1''')) MS:
(FI) 348 (M+, 100), 291 (12), 244 (5), 216 (6), 159 (13), 132 (19) IR:
(neat) 3467 (br), 2931 (s), 2858 (m), 1712 (m), 1462 (m), 1365 (m), 1255
(m), 1124 (m), 835 (s), 779 (s) TLC: Rf 0.13 (pentane/Et2O, 6/1,
anisaldehyde) Opt. Rot. : [α]D23 -17.8⁰ (c = 1.00, CHCl3) SFC: t R
(2S,4R,5S)-41c, 5.7 min (Daicel Chiralpak AD, 1% MeOH in CO2, 150 bar, 40
°C, 3.0 mL min-1) Analysis: C20H32O3Si (348.56) Calculated: C, 68.92; H,
9.25% Found: C, 68.75; H, 9.20%
