$DATUM (±)-(E)-7-((4-methoxybenzyl)oxy)hept-2-en-5-yn-4-ol (16). To a solution
of 1-(4-Methoxy-benzyloxy)-2-propyne4 (3.68 g, 20.9 mmol) in anhydrous
THF (16.0 mL) at –78 °C was added n-BuLi (2.30 M in hexanes, 8.4 mL, 19.3
mmol). After stirring at –78 °C for 30 min, a solution of crotonaldehyde
(1.33 mL, 16.1 mmol) in anhydrous THF (16.0 mL) was added via syringe.
After additional 1.5 h at –78 °C, the reaction mixture was quenched with
saturated aqueous NH4Cl. The THF was removed in vacuo, and the resulting
mixture was diluted with water and CH2Cl2. After separation of phases,
the aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (twice). The combined organic
extracts were dried over Na2SO4 and the solvent was removed in vacuo. The
crude product was purified by flash chromatography (silica gel, gradient
94:6 to 50:50 hexanes:EtOAc). The alcohol 16 (3.63 g, 92%) as a pale
yellow oil. Data for 16: Rf = 0.22 (75:25 hexanes:EtOAc); IR (thin film)
3408, 2937, 2914, 2854, 1612, 1514, 1442, 1355, 1303, 1250, 1175, 1071,
1033, 964, 820 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.30–7.27 (m, 2H),
6.90-6.87 (m, 2H), 5.91 (ddq, J = 15.2, 6.6, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 5.64 (ddq, J =
15.2, 6.3, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 4.88 (dd, J = 6.1, 6.1 Hz, 1H), 4.53 (s, 2H),
4.20 (d, J = 1.7 Hz, 2H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 1.82 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1H), 1.74
(ddd, J = 6.6, 1.6, 1.0 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 159.4, 130.2
129.9, 129.8, 129.4, 128.8, 113.9 (2C), 86.2, 81.8, 71.3, 62.9, 57.1,
55.3, 17.6; HRMS (ESI-TOF) calculated for C15H18O3Na [M+Na+] 269.1154,
found 269.1153.
