$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative procedure for catalytic reductive aldol reaction of
α,β-unsaturated aldehydes (Table 1): A 10 mL flame-dried round bottom
flask was charged with 16.5 mg of [(cod)Rh(R)-binap]BF4 (0.018 mmol), and
500 μL of dichloroethane. The resulting solution was stirred at room
temperature for approximately one minute or until the rhodium complex was
fully dissolved. After the complex was fully dissolved, 62 μL of
diethylmethylsilane (0.428 mmol) was added to the mixture and the
reaction vessel stirred for 30 minutes. Next, 250 μL of dichloroethane
followed by 50 μL of phenyl acrylate (0.357 mmol) and 172 μL
2-methyl-2-butenal (1.78 mmol ) was added to the solution. The vessel was
then sealed and allowed to stir for 24 hours, after which time 0.5
equivalents of diethylmethylsilane (0.1785 mmol) was added and the
reaction was stirred an additional 24 h . Solvent was then evaporated
from the reaction and 1 mL each of THF, MeOH, and 4N HCl were added. This
mixture was stirred at room temperature for an additional 45 minutes.
Ethyl acetate was then used to extract the product (3 x 25 mL). The
combined organic layers were washed with a saturated aqueous sodium
bicarbonate solution (2 x 20 mL), dried over Na2SO4, and filtered. The
solvent was removed by rotary evaporation to yield crude product which
was purified via flash chromatography (16:1, 14:1 then 13:1 hexanes:ethyl
acetate). 71 mg of a 2.5:1 ratio of
(2R,3R)-3-hydroxy-2,4-dimethyl-hex-4-ene-onic acid phenyl ester. IR (KBr)
3550 (br, m ) 2990 (m), 1780 (s), 1490 (m) 1200 (s) cm-1; 1H NMR : δ
7.5-6.98 (5H, m, aromatic), 5.61 (1H, br q, J=6.8 Hz, vinyl CH), 4.36
(1H, d, J=5.9 Hz, CHOH), 2.90 (1H, m, CH3CH), 2.06 (1H, br d, J=3.2 Hz,
OH), 1.68 (3H, s, vinyl CH 3), 1.65 (3H, s, vinyl CH 3), 1.32 (3H, d,
J=7.0 Hz, CHCH 3); 13C NMR: δ 174.2, 151.0, 135.5, 129.8,126.3,
122.4,121.9, 78.2,43.9, 30.1, 14.8, 13.5,12.4. HRMS Calc'd for C14H18O3
[M+H]+: 235.1334, Found: 235.1323.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, addnl. silane added after 24 h in stage 2, syn ee 75%,
aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Investigation of the Rh-Catalyzed Asymmetric Reductive Aldol Reaction.
Expanded Scope Based on Reaction Analysis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
