$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Nucleophilic
Pentafluoroethylation of Carbonyl Compounds with PhSO2CF2CF3. Under argon
atmosphere, into a 50 mL Schlenk flask containing a mixture of
benzaldehyde (69 mg, 0.65 mmol) and PhSO2CF2CF3 (1, 260mg, 1 mmol) in THF
(5 mL) at -75 °C was added dropwise a solution of t-BuOK (336mg, 3 mmol)
in THF (4 mL). The reaction mixture was then stirred vigorously at -75 to
-70 °C for 1.5 h, followed by quenching with 30 mL 2% aqueous HCl keeping
the same temperature. The solution mixture was extracted with Et2O (25 mL
x 3), and the combined organic phase was rinsed with saturated NaHCO3
solution (15 mL), brine solution (15 mL) and water (15 mL x 2)
subsequently and then dried over MgSO4. After the removal of volatile
solvents under vacuum, the crude product was further purified by
recrystallization with hexane (2 mL) at -50 °C to give
1-phenyl-2,2,3,3,3-pentafluoro-1-propanol (6a, 133 mg, 91%) as a pale
yellow solid. 4,4,5,5,5-Pentafluoro-1-phenyl-1-penten-3-ol (6d): pale
yellow oil. Yield 89% 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 2.65 (br, 1H); 4.75 (dt, 3JH, F =
15.0 Hz, 3JH, F, 3JH, H = 7.6 Hz, 1H); 6.25 (dd, 3JH, H = 15.9 Hz, 3JH, H
= 7.6 Hz, 1H); 6.85 (d, J= 15.9 Hz, 1H); 7.33-7.47 (m, 5H). 13C NMR
(CDCl3): δ 71.1 (dd, J= 26.8 Hz, 23.8 Hz); 113.2 (tq, J= 257.1 Hz, 35.3
Hz); 119.0 (qt, J= 286.0 Hz, 35.3 Hz); 120.2; 126.9; 128.7; 128.8; 135.3;
136.7.19F NMR (CDCl3): δ - 81.8 (s, 3F); -124.2 (dd, J= 274.9 Hz, 7.6 Hz,
1F); -129.1 (dd, J= 274.9 Hz, 15.0 Hz, 1F).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nucleophilic Perfluoroalkylation of Imines and Carbonyls: Perfluoroalkyl
Sulfones as Efficient Perfluoroalkyl-Transfer Motifs
