$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of 3,5-dimethoxybenzaldehyde (1.62 g, 9.77 mmol) in dry THF
(17 mL) was dropwise added vinylmagnesium bromide (1.0 M in THF, 12.5 mL,
12.5 mmol) at 0 °C. The solution was allowed to warm to room temperature
and stirred for 2 h. The reaction mixture was quenched with saturated
aqueous NH4Cl and extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined organic layer was
washed with water, dried, and concentrated in vacuo gave the brown liquid
which was subsequently purified by flash chromatography using silica gel
(14% EtOAc/Hexanes) to afford the alcohol (1.60 g, 84%) as a light
yellowish liquid. yield 1.60 g, 84% 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 6.54 (d, J
= 2.4 Hz, 2H), 6.38 (t, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H), 6.02 (ddd, J = 17.2, 10.4, 6.0
Hz, 1H), 5.36 (dt, J = 17.2, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 5.20 (dt, J = 10.4, 1.2 Hz,
1H), 5.14 (br t, J = 4.8 Hz, 1H), 3.79 (s, 6H), 1.99-1.97 (m, 1H)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
