$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Baylis-Hillman
reaction: Enantioselective Baylis-Hillman Reaction Employing 10. To a 10
mL round bottom flask, flame dried and equipped with a stir bar, was
added peptide 10 (0.0015 mmol), dissolved in CHCl3/THF (1:2, 0.5M),
L-proline (0.0015 mmol), aldehyde 1 (0.015 mmol), and methyl vinyl ketone
(0.029 mmol). The resulting mixture was stirred until complete loss of
starting material was observed by TLC (2:1 hexanes/ethyl acetate). The
reaction was diluted with chloroform and purification via flash
chromatography (SiO2, CHCl3). 2.7 mg (81%) of 2 as a pale yellow oil.
3-(Furan-2-yl-hydroxy-methyl)-but-3-en-2-one (23). 1 H NMR (CDCl3, 400
MHz) δ 7.36 (s, 1H), 6.34-6.32 (m, 1H), 6.25-6.24 (m, 2H), 6.1 (s, 1H),
5.63 (d, J = 5.8 Hz, 1H), 3.26 (bs, 1H), 2.38 (s, 3H); 13 C NMR (CDCl3,
100 MHz) δ 199.2, 154.2, 147.2, 141.6, 126.4, 109.9, 106.6, 65.2, 25.7;
IR (film, cm-1) 3320, 2957, 2923, 2852, 1714, 1667, 1510, 1462, 1376; TLC
R f 0.56 (30% ethyl acetate/hexanes); [α]D -6.5 (0.31, CHCl3, 63% ee);
Exact mass calcd for [C9H10O3 + Na]+ requires m/z 189.0528. Found
189.0526 (ESI+). Assay of enantiomeric purity: Enantiomers of product
were separated by chiral HPLC employing a Chiralcel AD column (Diacel).
Conditions: 95:5 hexanes:ethanol; Flow rate 0.75 mL/min; 29.0 min (major
ent), 37.0 min (minor ent).
