$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
β,β-Difluorinated Homoallylic Alcohol Derivatives A vigorously stirred
suspension of indium powder (1.38 g, 12.0 mmol), aldehyde (10.0 mmol),
DMF (20.0 mL) was cooled to 0°C in an ice bath, and
3-bromo-3,3-difluoropropene (1.88 g, 12.0 mmol) was slowly added via a
dropping funnel. After the addition was completed, the reaction mixture
was allowed to warm to room temperature and stirring was continued
overnight. To work up, 10% aqueous hydrochloric acid (30.0 mL) was added
to the reaction mixture, and excess indium were removed by suction
filtration and the residues were washed with ether (30.0 mL). The organic
layer was separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with ether (2 x
50.0 mL). The combined organic extracts were washed with brine (50.0 mL),
then dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate, filtered and concentrated in
vacuo. The residues were purified by column chromatography. The desired
compound. methyl 4-(2,2-difluoro-1-hydroxybut-3-enyl)benzoate (1h’)
2,2-difluoro-1-(thiophen-2-yl)but-3-en-1-ol (1k’) Prepared from methyl
thiophene-2-carbaldehyde using general procedure to afford 1k’ as a
colorless oil (1.52 g, 80%). (elution: 15% EtOAc/petrol; Rf = 0.4 w/ 30%
EtOAc/petrol). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, 293 K, TMS): δ ppm 7.31-6.97 (m,
3H), 5.99-5.82 (m, 1H), 5.68-5.46 (m, 2H), 5.09 (t, J = 9.3 Hz, 1H), 2.98
(br, 1H). 19F NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3): δ ppm -108.0 (AB, J AB = 247.0 Hz, 3
J HF = 10.4 Hz, 1F), -109.4 (AB, J AB = 247.0 Hz, 3 J HF = 10.2 Hz, 1F).
13C NMR (100.7 MHz, CDCl3, 293 K, TMS): δ ppm 138.8, 129.2 (t, J = 25.5
Hz), 126.9, 126.8, 126.3, 122.1 (t, J = 9.5 Hz), 119.1 (t, J = 242.8 Hz),
72.5 (t, J = 31.3 Hz). IR (thin film): υmax 3438, 3107, 2893, 1421, 1224,
1160, 1066, 995, 956, 858, 808, 761, 708 cm-1. MS (EI) : m/z (%) 190
(M+), 113, 85 (100), 77, 45. HRMS (EI-TOF) Calculated for C8H8F2OS:
190.0264. Found: 190.0264.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium-catalyzed anti-Markovnikov hydroalkylation of homoallylic
alcohols bearing β-fluorines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lin, Xiaowei; Qing, Feng-Ling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(17), 4478-4481

