$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the synthesis of syn
α-vinyl-β-hydroxy esters 3. To a 0 °C solution of borohydride 6R (81 mg,
0.250 mmol, 1 equiv, considering a 90% yield for the conversion of
borohydride 6R to borane 1R based on titration3) in CH2Cl2 (0.5 mL) was
added TMSCl (32 μL, 0.250 mmol, 1 equiv). The reaction mixture was
stirred at 0 °C for 10 min, then a solution of allene ester 24 (0.325
mmol, 1.3 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL) was added. The reaction mixture was
stirred at 0 °C for 1h, then was cooled to -78 °C and benzaldehyde (18
μL, 0.175 mmol, 0.7 equiv) was added. The mixture was stirred at -78 °C
for 12h before a pH 7 buffer solution (KH2SO4/NaOH) (1 mL), THF (1.5 mL)
and MeOH (0.5 mL) were added. The heterogeneous solution was allowed to
warm to 20 °C and was stirred vigorously for 6h. The mixture was poured
into a saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution and was extracted with EtOAc
(3x). The combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried over
MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by flash column chromatography (SiO2, hexanes / EtOAc, gradient
elution). syn α-vinyl-β-hydroxy esters 3a-g. (2R,3S,E)-Ethyl
3-hydroxy-5-phenyl-2-vinylpent-4-enoate (3e). Colorless oil; Yield 79%;
syn/anti >40:1; ee 78%. [α]D 25 = + 10.1 (c 0.76, CHCl3); 1H (400 MHz,
CDCl3) 7.36-7.20 (m, 5H), 6.63 (d, J = 15.9 Hz, 1H), 6.17 (dd, J = 15.9,
6.8 Hz, 1H), 5.96 (ddd, J = 17.2, 10.4 , 9.1 Hz, 1H), 5.31 (dd, J = 10.4,
1.0 Hz, 1H), 5.26 (dt, J = 17.2, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 4.57 (t, J = 6.1 Hz, 1H),
4.15 (q, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 3.23 (dd, J = 8.8, 5.6 Hz, 1H), 2.76 (bs, 1H),
1.22 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H); 13C (100 MHz, CDCl3) 172.7, 136.7, 132.3,
132.0, 128.8, 128.4, 128.0, 126.8, 120.7, 73.1, 61.3, 56.8, 14.4; IR
(neat) 3444, 2981, 2928, 1728, 1715, 1448, 1369, 1244, 1178, 1096, 1026,
966, 923, 750, 693 cm-1; HRMS (EI) calcd for C15H18O3 [M]+ 246.1256,
found 246.1240.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (stage 2), stereoselective (stage 3), buffered solution
(KHSO4/NaOH in last stage), more than 40:1 syn:anti, 78%ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantio- and Diastereoselective Synthesis of syn-β-Hydroxy-α-vinyl
Carboxylic Esters via Reductive Aldol Reactions of Ethyl
Allenecarboxylate with 10-TMS-9-Borabicyclo[3.3.2]decane and DFT Analysis
of the Hydroboration Pathway
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kister, Jeremy; Ess, Daniel H.; Roush, William R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(21), 5436-5439

