$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Methoxycarbonyl-4-methyl-5-phenyl-4,7-octadien-1-yn-3-ol (4g); To a
solution of diisopropylamine (10.00 mmol) in THF (25.0 mL) was added
n-BuLi (1.5 M solution in n-pentane, 10.0 mmol) at -78 °C. After 10 min,
a solution of methyl propiolate (10.0 mmol) in THF was added to the
mixture at the same temperature. After stirring for 10 min, a solution of
2-methyl-3-phenyl-2,5-hexadienal (10) (4.00 mmol) in THF was added to the
mixture and the mixture was stirred for 10 min at the same temperature.
The reaction mixture was then quenched by addition of aqueous NH4Cl and
extracted three times with Et2O. The organic layers were combined, dried
over Na2SO4, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The resulting
residue was purified by silica gel flash column chromatography
(hexane/EtOAc = 3/1) (75% yield). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.74 (s, 3H), 2.56 (d,
J = 4.6 Hz, 1H), 3.17 (ddd, J = 15.9, 6.4, 0.6 Hz, 1H), 3.22 (ddd, J =
15.8, 5.8, 0.6 Hz, 1H), 3.79 (s, 3H), 5.02 (dq, J = 10.1, 1.8 Hz, 1H),
5.05 (dq, J = 17.1, 1.9 Hz, 1H), 5.56 (d, J = 4.6 Hz, 1H), 5.76 (ddt, J =
17.1, 10.1, 6.1 Hz, 1H), 7.12-7.14 (m, 2H), 7.23-7.26 (m, 1H), 7.30-7.34
(m, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 14.73, 38.52, 52.79, 61.77, 76.29, 86.89,
116.02, 126.76, 128.08, 128.25, 130.13, 134.93, 137.79, 142.15, 153.80;
HRMS (FAB) calcd for C17H18O3K (M++K) 309.0893, found 309.0881.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Styrenes Using Ruthenium-Catalyzed Ring-Closing Enyne
