$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure B: To a stirred solution of
the exocyclic enol ether (1.20 mmol) and the carbonyl derivative (1.00
mmol) in 1.5 mL THF was added zinc(II)chloride (0.5 mL of a 0.4 M
solution in THF, 0.2 mmol) dropwise. After the time specified in Table 2,
the reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo and the residue purified
directly by flash column chromatography. Dihydropyran 20: The reaction of
2-methylenetetrahydropyran (1), and 2,3-butanedione (9) was conducted
according to the general procedure B. The crude residue was purified by
flash chromatography (SiO2; CH2Cl2:ethyl acetate, 10:1 → 2:1; with 5%
triethylamine). Dihydropyran 25: The reaction of
2-methylenetetrahydropyran (1), and cinnamaldehyde (14) was conducted
according to the general procedure B. The crude residue was purified by
flash chromatography (SiO2; CH2Cl2:ethyl acetate, 100:1 → 2:1; with 5%
triethylamine). Dihydropyran 25 (75%) as a pale yellow oil. TLC: R f =
0.68 (hexanes: EtOAc, 2:1). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ 7.31 (5H, m), 6.64
(1H, dd, J = 15.9, 1.0 Hz), 6.23 (1H, dd, J = 15.9, 6.1 Hz), 4.64 (1H, t,
J = 3.7 Hz), 4.49 (1H, m), 4.03 (2H, m), 2.58 (1H, d, J = 3.0 Hz), 2.39
(1H, ddd, J = 14.2, 3.8, 0.7 Hz), 2.26 (1H, dd, J = 14.2, 8.3 Hz), 2.04
(2H, m), 1.82 (2H, m). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ 150.8, 136.7, 131.5,
129.4, 128.2 (2C), 127.1, 126.2 (2C), 98.3, 70.3, 65.9, 42.4, 22.0, 19.9.
IR (film): 3436, 3025, 2928, 1676 cm-1. HRMS (ESI) Calcd for C15H18O2
([M+Na]+): 253.1199, found: 253.1197.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
