$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Grignard Addition to Aldehyde (Step 2, for 1e
& 1f): To a solution of the crude aldehyde C (0.39 g, 2.0 mmol) in dry
THF (10 mL) at -10°C was added slowly Grignard reagent (2.2 mmol). The
reaction was allowed to warm to r.t. over 60 min, and quenched with water
(10 mL). The organic layer was collected and the aqueous layer was
extracted with ethyl acetate (3 x 10 mL). The combined organic fractions
were washed with brine, dried over anhydrous MgSO4 and concentrated under
reduced pressure to give the crude substituted furfuryl alcohol D, which
was used without further purification for the next step. DIBAL-H
Reduction of Ester (Step 3, for 1b, 1e & 1f): To a solution of the crude
alcohol (D or E, 2.0 mmol) in dry DCM (5 mL) at 0oC was added
diisobutylaluminium hydride (DIBAL-H, 7.2 mL, 1 M, 7.2 mmol) dropwise.
The reaction was allowed to warm to r.t. and stirred for another 2 hrs.
The reaction was then quenched by sequential addition of H2O (0.29 mL),
15% aqueous NaOH (0.29 mL) and H2O (0.72 mL). The resulting reaction
mixture was stirred at r.t. for 30 min, and anhydrous MgSO4 was added.
After filtration, the filtrate was collected and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The crude residue was purified by flash column
chromatography on silica gel (ethyl acetate/hexane=1:1) to give the
corresponding pure substituted furfuryl alcohols 1b4, 1e & 1f. 1f:
Colorless oil, yield 86% over 3 steps. IR (neat, cm-1): 3346, 3078, 2940,
2879, 1643, 1560, 1434, 1055, 1012, 917, 786; 1H NMR (400 MHz, C6D6) δ :
6.06 (d, J =3.2 Hz, 1H), 5.84 (d, J =3.2 Hz, 1H), 5.81 (m, 1H), 5.04 (m,
2H), 4.60 (t, J =6.4 Hz, 2H), 3.45 (t, J =6.4 Hz, 2H), 2.60 (m, 4H), 1.74
(m, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, C6D6) δ : 155.45, 155.40, 134.8, 117.6, 106.9,
105.8, 67.4, 61.6, 40.5, 31.3, 24.7; HRMS (CI+) m/z calculated for
C11H16O3 [M]+ 196.1099, found 196.1099.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Grignard reaction (stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Diastereoselective Reductive Ring Expansion of Spiroketal
Dihydropyranones to cis-Fused Bicyclic Ethers
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhu, Liangyu; Song, Liyan; Tong, Rongbiao
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(23), 5892-5895

