$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (1R,3R)-1,5-Diphenyl-2-vinyl-pentane-1,3-diol (20): To a mixture of
allene 19 (30 mg, 0.16 mmol) and 1Ipc2BH6 (52.9 mg, 0.186 mmol) was added
Et2O (0.66 mL) at 0°C. The heterogeneous mixture was stirred vigorously
for 10 min to form in situ the (Z)- allyborane and cooled to -78°C.
Benzaldehyde (13.5 μL, 0.133 mmol) was slowly added dropwise and stirring
was continued for 1 h. MeOH (0.5 mL) was then added at -78°C and the
reaction was stirred for 2 h. The mixture was then concentrated under
reduced pressure, and the crude residue was chromatographed twice (10:90
ethyl acetate/hexanes) to give benzyl alcohol 20 (33 mg, 84%) as an
inseparable 1.3 (isomer A):1 (isomer B) mixture of diastereomers
(1R,3R)-1,5-Diphenyl-2-vinyl-pentane-1,3-diol (20), yield 33 mg, 84% [α]D
22.0 = +12.8° (c = 1.35, CHCl3); 1H NMR δ 7.34-7.06 (m, 20H), 6.00 (ddd,
J= 10.4, 10.4, 17.6 Hz, 1H-B), 5.35 (ddd, J= 10.4, 10.4, 17.2 Hz, 1H-A),
5.32 (d, J= 10.4 Hz, 1H-B), 5.07 (dd, J= 2.0, 17.6, 1H-B), 4.98 (dd, J=
1.6, 10.0 Hz, 1HA), 4.90 (dd, J=1.6, 17.2-A), 4.87 (dd, J= 1.2, 6.0 Hz,
1H-B), 4.82 (dd, J= 2.8, 8.0 Hz, 1H-A), 3.92 (d, J= 2.8 Hz, 1H-A), 3.50
(ddd, J= 3.6, 3.6, 8.4 Hz, 1H-A), 3.47 (s, 3H-A), 3.28 (s, 3H-B), 3.12
(ddd, J= 2.0, 4.0, 8.8 Hz, 1H-B), 2.99 (d, J= 1.2 Hz, 1H-B), 2.80- 2.52
(m, 4H), 2.45-2.35 (m, 2H), 2.05-1.88 (m, 2H), 1.83-1.63 (m, 2H); 13C NMR
δ 142.8, 142.7, 142.7, 141.9, 135.0, 133.9, 128.7, 128.6, 128.5, 128.5,
128.3, 128.3, 127.8, 127.7, 127.5, 127.1, 126.2, 126.1, 121.0, 119.2,
82.8, 82.3, 76.9, 75.8, 57.2, 56.7, 55.9, 54.4, 32.5, 32.2, 31.8, 29.8;
IR (thin film) 3440, 3060, 3027, 2929, 1638, 1603, 1494, 1454, 1195,
1089, 1028, 995, 916, 764, 752, 722, 699 cm-1; HRMS (ESI) calcd for
C20H24O2 (M+Na)+ 319.1669, found 319.1660 m/z.
